{"abstract":"In the Vertex Connectivity Survivable Network Design (VC-SNDP) problem, the input is a graph G and a function d : V (G) × V (G) → N that encodes the vertex-connectivity demands between pairs of vertices. The objective is to find the smallest subgraph H of G that satisfies all these demands. It is a well-studied NP-complete problem that generalizes several network design problems. We consider the case of uniform demands, where for every vertex pair (u, v) the connectivity demand d(u, v) is a fixed integer κ. It is an important problem with wide applications. We study this problem in the realm of Parameterized Complexity. In this setting, in addition to G and d we are given an integer ℓ as the parameter and the objective is to determine if we can remove at least ℓ edges from G without violating any connectivity constraints. This was posed as an open problem by Bang-Jansen et.al. [SODA 2018], who studied the edge-connectivity variant of the problem under the same settings. Using a powerful classification result of Lokshtanov et al. [ICALP 2018], Gutin et al. [JCSS 2019] recently showed that this problem admits a (non-uniform) FPT algorithm where the running time was unspecified. Further they also gave an (uniform) FPT algorithm for the case of κ = 2. In this paper we present a (uniform) FPT algorithm any κ that runs in time 2O(κ2ℓ4 log ℓ) · |V (G)|O(1). Our algorithm is built upon new insights on vertex connectivity in graphs. Our main conceptual contribution is a novel graph decomposition called the Wheel decomposition. Informally, it is a partition of the edge set of a graph G, E(G) = X1 ∪ X2 . . . ∪ Xr, with the parts arranged in a cyclic order, such that each vertex v ∈ V (G) either has edges in at most two consecutive parts, or has edges in every part of this partition. The first kind of vertices can be thought of as the rim of the wheel, while the second kind form the hub. Additionally, the vertex cuts induced by these edge-sets in G have highly symmetric properties. Our main technical result, informally speaking, establishes that “nearly edge-minimal” κ-vertex connected graphs admit a wheel decomposition – a fact that can be exploited for designing algorithms. We believe that this decomposition is of independent interest and it could be a useful tool in resolving other open problems.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Bang-Jensen, Jørgen","Klinkby, Kristine Vitting","Misra, Pranabendu","Saurabh, Saket"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-702831"],"event":{"end":"2023-09-06","place":"Amsterdam, nl","start":"2023-09-04","title":"31st Annual European Symposium on Algorithms, ESA 2023","year":"2023"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, South","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Bang-Jensen, Jørgen"],"country":["India","Norway"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Chennai Mathematical Institute","Institute of Mathematical Sciences India","University of Bergen"],"keyword":["Network design","Parameterized complexity","Vertex Connectivity"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a parameterized algorithm for vertex connectivity survivable network design problem with uniform demands","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.4230/LIPIcs.ESA.2023.13","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["Funding Pranabendu Misra: Supported by Google India Research Award 2022, and Start-Up Grant 2022 (SRG/2022/001927) of Science and Engineering Research Board (SERB), India. Saket Saurabh: Supported by the European Research Council (ERC) under the European Union’s Horizon 2020 research and innovation programme (grant agreement No. 819416), and Swarnajayanti Fellowship (No. DST/SJF/MSA01/2017-18)."],"id":"S01-000.00-702831","identifier":[{"id":"85173474567","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-096a7e06-80d2-4752-a93a-9d64d5517997"],"keyword":["Network Design","Parameterized Complexity","Vertex Connectivity"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-2B422960B57536CEF673082F39E6EA76"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.4230/LIPIcs.ESA.2023.13","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/243676636/LIPIcs_ESA_2023_13.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, Faculty of Science, Department of Mathematics and Computer Science","SDU, Faculty of Science, Department of Mathematics and Computer Science, Algorithms"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"in","key":"chennai mathematical institute","loc":["India","Asia, South"],"name":"Chennai Mathematical Institute","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"in","key":"institute of mathematical sciences india","loc":["India","Asia, South"],"name":"Institute of Mathematical Sciences India","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"no","key":"university of bergen","loc":["Norway","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"University of Bergen","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jørgen","key":"bangjensenpau","last":"Bang-Jensen","locid":"98e7ba05-a95c-4fee-9045-5c47b60c4e8a","name":"Bang-Jensen, Jørgen","orcid":"0000-0001-5783-7125","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Kristine Vitting","key":"klinkbypau","last":"Klinkby","locid":"61b2437d-6b15-44c3-a218-5efa09a15099","name":"Klinkby, Kristine Vitting","orcid":"0000-0002-5917-9354","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Pranabendu","key":"misrapau","last":"Misra","name":"Misra, Pranabendu","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 4","corresponding":null,"first":"Saket","key":"saurabhpau","last":"Saurabh","name":"Saurabh, Saket","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Inge","key":"ligortzpedh","last":"Li Gortz","name":"Li Gortz, Inge","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Martin","key":"farachcoltonpedh","last":"Farach-Colton","name":"Farach-Colton, Martin","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Simon J.","key":"puglisipedh","last":"Puglisi","name":"Puglisi, Simon J.","rank":7,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Grzegorz","key":"hermanpedh","last":"Herman","name":"Herman, Grzegorz","rank":8,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.4230/lipics.esa.2023.13","eisbn":["9783959772952"],"issn":["18688969"],"publisher":"Schloss Dagstuhl- Leibniz-Zentrum fur Informatik GmbH, Dagstuhl Publishing","series":"Leibniz International Proceedings in Informatics, LIPIcs","status":"p","title":"31st Annual European Symposium on Algorithms, ESA 2023"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85173474567"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-096a7e06-80d2-4752-a93a-9d64d5517997"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"A Parameterized Algorithm for Vertex Connectivity Survivable Network Design Problem with Uniform Demands","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-702831","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Augmenting an undirected or a directed graph (digraph) by adding new edges or arcs, to increase its connectivity to a target value, is a fundamental problem in combinatorial optimization and graph theory. In this paper we study the basic problem of augmenting an input digraph to make it strongly connected, which is known as the Strong Connectivity Augmentation problem. Here, the input is a digraph D = (V, A), a set of links L ⊆ V × V, and a positive integer k. The objective is to decide if there exists a subset F ⊆ L, of size at most k, such that D0 = (V, A ∪ F) is strongly connected. We consider the general version of this problem where, additionally, there is a weight function w : L → R+ on the links, and the goal is to find a minimum weight subset F ⊆ L of cardinality at most k, such that D0 = (V, A∪F) is strongly connected. We design an algorithm for this problem that runs in time 2O(k log k)nO(1), thereby showing that it is fixed parameter tractable (FPT). Here, n = |V |. This also resolves an open problem stated by Guo and Uhlmann more than a decade ago [ Networks 56(2): 131-142 (2010)].","author_count":4,"contributors":["Klinkby, Kristine Vitting","Misra, Pranabendu","Saurabh, Saket"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-637677"],"event":{"end":"2021-01-13","place":"Alexandria, Virtual, us","start":"2021-01-10","title":"32nd Annual ACM-SIAM Symposium on Discrete Algorithms, SODA 2021","year":"2021"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, South","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Klinkby, Kristine Vitting"],"country":["Germany","India","Norway"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Institute of Mathematical Sciences India","Max Planck Institute for Informatics","University of Bergen"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"strong connectivity augmentation is fpt","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85105353325","version":"Other Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["∗UniversityofBergen, Norway, andUniversityofSouthern Denmark, Odense, Denmark. kristine.knudsen@ii.uib.no †Max-PlanckInstituteforInformatics, SIC,Saarbrucken, Germany.pmisra@mpi-inf.mpg.de ‡TheInstituteofMathematicalSciences, HBNI,Chennai, India, and University of Bergen, Norway. saket@imsc.res.in Saket Saurabhissupportedbyfundingfrom theEuropeanResearchCouncil(ERC) under theEuropeanUnion’sHorizon2020research andinnovation programme(grantagreement No. 819416)andalsoacknowledgesthe supportofSwarnajayanti Fellowship grant DST/SJF/MSA-01/2017-18."],"id":"S01-000.00-637677","identifier":[{"id":"85105353325","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-e10d81a3-691a-4fb3-bd5f-3d969691eb3a"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-5A427EF46923CD5FB9F302396C08C98D"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, Faculty of Science, Department of Mathematics and Computer Science","SDU, Faculty of Science, Department of Mathematics and Computer Science, Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"de","key":"max planck institute for informatics","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Max Planck Institute for Informatics","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"no","key":"university of bergen","loc":["Norway","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"University of Bergen","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"in","key":"institute of mathematical sciences india","loc":["India","Asia, South"],"name":"Institute of Mathematical Sciences India","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Kristine Vitting","key":"klinkbypau","last":"Klinkby","locid":"61b2437d-6b15-44c3-a218-5efa09a15099","name":"Klinkby, Kristine Vitting","orcid":"0000-0002-5917-9354","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Pranabendu","key":"misrapau","last":"Misra","name":"Misra, Pranabendu","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 4","corresponding":null,"first":"Saket","key":"saurabhpau","last":"Saurabh","name":"Saurabh, Saket","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Dániel","key":"marxpedh","last":"Marx","name":"Marx, Dániel","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1137/1.9781611976465.15","eisbn":["9781611976465"],"pages":"219-234","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","series":"Proceedings of the Annual ACM-SIAM Symposium on Discrete Algorithms","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 2021 ACM-SIAM Symposium on Discrete Algorithms (SODA)"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85105353325"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-e10d81a3-691a-4fb3-bd5f-3d969691eb3a"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Strong connectivity augmentation is FPT","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-637677","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"In the Survivable Network Design Problem (SNDP), the input is an edge-weighted (di)graph G and an integer ruυ for every pair of vertices u, υ ∊ V(G). The objective is to construct a subgraph H of minimum weight which contains ruυ edge-disjoint (or node-disjoint) u-υ paths. This is a fundamental problem in combinatorial optimization that captures numerous well-studied problems in graph theory and graph algorithms. Consequently, there is a long line of research into exact-polynomial time algorithms as well as approximation algorithms for various restrictions of this problem. An important restriction of this problem is one where the connectivity demands are the same for every pair of vertices. In this paper, we first consider the edge-connectivity version of this problem which we call λ-Edge Connected Subgraph (λ-ECS). In this problem, the input is a λ-edge connected (di)graph G and an integer k and the objective is to check whether G contains a spanning subgraph H that is also λ-edge connected and H excludes at least k edges of G. In other words, we are asked to compute a maximum subset of edges, of cardinality at least k, which may be safely deleted from G without affecting its connectivity. If we replace λ-edge connectivity with λ-vertex connectivity we get the λ-Vertex Connected Subgraph (λ-VCS) problem. We show that λ-ECS is fixed-parameter tractable (FPT) for both graphs and digraphs even if the (di)graph has nonnegative real weights on the edges and the objective is to exclude from H, some edges of G whose total weight exceeds a prescribed value. In particular, we design an algorithm for the weighted variant of the problem with running time 2O(k log k) |V(G)|O(1). We follow up on this result and obtain a polynomial compression for λ-ECS on unweighted graphs. As a direct consequence of our results, we obtain the first FPT algorithm for the parameterized version of the classical Minimum Equivalent Graph (MEG) problem. We also show that λ-Ves is FPT on digraphs; however the problem on undirected graphs remains open. Finally, we complement our algorithmic findings by showing that SNDP is W[1]-hard for both arc and vertex connectivity versions on digraphs. The core of our algorithms is composed of new combinatorial results on connectivity in digraphs and undirected graphs.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Bang-Jensen, Jørgen","Klinkby Knudsen, Kristine Vitting","Saurabh, Saket","Basavaraju, Manu","Misra, Pranabendu","Zehavi, Meirav","Ramanujan, M.S."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-635278"],"event":{"acronym":"SODA","end":"2018-01-10","place":"New Orleans, us","start":"2018-01-07","title":"Twenty-Ninth Annual ACM-SIAM Symposium on Discrete Algorithms (SODA) 2-018","year":"2018"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, Middle East","Asia, South","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["India","Israel","Norway","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Ben-Gurion University of the Negev","Institute of Mathematical Sciences India","University of Bergen","University of Warwick"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"parameterized algorithms for survivable network design with uniform demands","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85045548969","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-635278","identifier":[{"id":"85045548969","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-d8adbb94-2e9e-4ad5-afe5-15003d0ab663"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-C85F5A12795BA079C70D53EF274CF85C"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, Faculty of Science, Department of Mathematics and Computer Science","SDU, Faculty of Science, Department of Mathematics and Computer Science, Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"no","key":"university of bergen","loc":["Norway","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"University of Bergen","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"in","key":"institute of mathematical sciences india","loc":["India","Asia, South"],"name":"Institute of Mathematical Sciences India","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"gb","key":"university of warwick","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Warwick","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"il","key":"ben gurion university of the negev","loc":["Israel","Asia, Middle East","OECD"],"name":"Ben-Gurion University of the Negev","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jørgen","key":"bangjensenpau","last":"Bang-Jensen","locid":"98e7ba05-a95c-4fee-9045-5c47b60c4e8a","name":"Bang-Jensen, Jørgen","orcid":"0000-0001-5783-7125","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Kristine Vitting","key":"klinkbyknudsenpau","last":"Klinkby Knudsen","name":"Klinkby Knudsen, Kristine Vitting","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Saket","key":"saurabhpau","last":"Saurabh","name":"Saurabh, Saket","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Manu","key":"basavarajupau","last":"Basavaraju","name":"Basavaraju, Manu","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Pranabendu","key":"misrapau","last":"Misra","name":"Misra, Pranabendu","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"first":"Meirav","key":"zehavipau","last":"Zehavi","name":"Zehavi, Meirav","rank":6,"rolecode":